WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.602
-Congratulations on winning.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:05.471
-This is the trophy right here.
Do you mind if I bring it up?

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.605
-That's good.

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:08.007
-Wow! It's actually
really heavy.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:09.208
Look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.644
♪♪
Yeah.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.646
-Yeah, just set it right there.
-That's really heavy.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.650
-Yeah.
-Wow. What a great trophy.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.118
What are you
going to do with this?

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.219
-Probably hang
it up somewhere or,

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.353
like, put it on, like,
one of my desks.

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:22.422
-You can't hang this thing.
It's 100 pounds.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.656
-Yeah, yeah, I can't hang --

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.258
-You have to lean it against --
It's so heavy.

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:30.063
You got to build
a whole new room around it.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.831
I want to put
this over here just for now

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.234
so I can see your face,
because it's giant.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.569
Explain this to me.
How does it work?

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.670
What goes into it?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.105
Because I think people think,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.907
"Oh, you just play
video games and you won."

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.275
It's like, no,
I think there's --

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.275
You put a lot of work into this.

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:44.276
-Yeah.
-Am I right?

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.312
-So, like,
long practice every day.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.414
Like, every day, I wake up,
got to, like,

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.882
warm up my hands for 30 minutes.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:52.719
Then I got to pretty much,
like, you know, play --

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.053
warm up my hands
by playing, like,

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.888
"Fortnite Creative,"
stuff like that.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:56.956
-So, wait.
Walk me through your day.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.758
So, what time do you wake up?

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:02.395
-We talking school day
or a weekend?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.831
-Let's talk weekend.
-Okay.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:11.004
-Yeah.
-Maybe like 12:00, 1:00.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.573
-Oh, man.
I want to be you so bad, dude.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.342
I'm really -- I'm so jealous.
I'm so jealous of you right now.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.344
So, you wake up
at 12:00 noon, yeah?

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.279
And before you warm up
your hands, what do you do?

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:23.316
Yeah. What do you eat?
What do you eat at 12:00 noon?

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.785
-Maybe a banana.
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.186
All right, I like bananas.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.655
-So, you get a --
But then you get on to the game

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:31.591
and you start playing
immediately or no?

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.958
-Yeah, I, like, get on,
warm up with that,

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.394
and then I go into,
like, a call,

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:35.561
talk to, like,
my friends, and all that,

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.130
go over strategies and then --

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.499
-Do you play just strangers or
do you play with, like, a --

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.501
-No, like, a team, like, friends
and stuff like that, yeah.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.868
-You're on a team now.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.771
-What is the name of your team?
-Sentinels.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.339
-Sentinels. Yeah, so,
you get on with those guys

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.074
and you --
It's Monday through --

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.408
It's every day or what is it?

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:50.876
-Pretty much, yeah.
It's like my job.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:52.211
-That's -- Wow.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:54.013
And did your parents --
I know they're proud of you,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.749
but, at first,
were they like...

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.783
I mean, yeah.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:58.985
But, at first,
they got to be like,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.787
"Hey, we got to talk, Bugha."

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.189
You know, yeah, let's --"
What is Bugha from?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.692
-My grandpa gave me the name
when I was, like, a baby.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.026
He used to say like,
"Bugha, Bugha, Bugha,"

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.227
and I used to laugh.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:09.729
-Oh, no way.
-So that's where I get it from.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.365
-Hey, good for that.
I love grandpa stories.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.634
So, your parents
go, "Okay, this is fun,

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:18.604
but you got to get
working over at, like,

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.005
7-Eleven or something.

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:21.407
You got to get a job."

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.710
-Yeah, so, like, pretty much,
when they found out, like,

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.612
I could actually do this for
pretty much a job, like,

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:28.881
was when I pretty much got
signed to the team and all that.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.950
But before that, I just did,
like, little competitions

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.518
and made, like,
a little bit of money off that.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:34.820
-Like, how much money did you
win the first competition?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.323
-$100.
-Yeah, nothing.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.724
-Yeah, nothing.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:39.926
-What are you? 16? $100?

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.294
You must have
freaked out and said,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.762
"Mom, dad, this is something.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.796
I can make money.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.297
And they're like,
"It's only $100, buddy."

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:46.432
But that's a lot of money.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.533
-To me, it was at the time,
because, like --

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.835
-To me, it is now.
Yeah, I mean...

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.137
Wow, $100?

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:54.006
So you win 100 bucks and then
you go, "I can do this."

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:57.076
And then this happens.
I mean, did you freak out?

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.110
-I don't know.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.312
It's like I had, like,
no emotion,

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.646
but, at the same time,
it felt, like, unreal.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:01.980
I don't know.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.649
-Because you were just -- You
were just in the zone?

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:04.783
-Yeah, pretty much.

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.820
-So, what time of day was
this that you won?

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.821
-When it happened?
-Yeah.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.023
-Like midday yesterday.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.325
-Like when you wake up?
12:00 noon?

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:16.528
Yeah. Woke up, had a banana,
won $3 million.

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:20.966
No big deal. Not bad.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.836
So, I just -- I've got to
congratulate you on this.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.038
This is great.
This is a great trophy.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.672
And I hope to
see you again, buddy.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:27.874
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.608
-Good job.
-Appreciate it.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:32.078
-Kyle "Bugha" Giersdorf.

